<title>BAHRAIN: Bahrain stock exchange gets new acting director.</title>
<headline>Bahrain stock exchange gets new acting director.</headline>
<dateline>MANAMA 1997-06-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sheikh Ahmed bin Mohammed al-Khalifa has taken over as acting director of the Bahrain Stock Exchange, bourse officials said.</p>
<p>Sheikh Ahmed last week replaced former BSE director, Fawzi Behzad, who has been appointed as an adviser at the Commerce Ministry.</p>
<p>BSE officials said on Monday Sheikh Ahmed had worked as head of operations at the bourse before he was moved to the Finance Ministry last year.</p>
<p>Sheikh Ahmed, from Bahrain's al-Khalifa ruling family, took over his new post at the BSE last week, they said.</p>
<p>-- Bahrain newsroom 973-524424.</p>
</text>
